      "findings": [],
      "observations": [
        "Independent source-first pixels show one Oxy frame with B(1,2), A(3,5), C(6,1), exactly solid BA/BC, three dashed vertical projections, positive arrows, negative tails, and numbered 2/4/6 ticks.",
        "The complete current preview preserves every source point, branch, guide, unit tick, label, and origin. The x=3 guide crosses BC without a new point; no AC, area fill, horizontal guide, query point, graph extension, or coordinate caption is added.",
        "Applicable spec inventory groups require pointRelationships and cover all B/A/C with mapped in-group executable displacements. O is explicitly represented by origin-label at [0,0], the common axis intersection, and all three source-coordinate displacement origins; it is not an extra filled marker.",
        "The complete spec authoritativeText equals the current authored title/prose and complete exercise 320. Full context lesson and exercise objects equal the current templates. Both correspondence directions and interval [1,6] remain unchanged, without solving the question.",
        "Twelve visible labels are exactly 2,4,6 twice and A,B,C,O,x,y. Three source point markers are filled; the complete canvas shows clear labels and bounds. Visible text contains no Cyrillic or added answer annotation.",
        "Regular unit spacing, clean strokes, circular markers, enlarged type, semantic ink/muted color, and regularized blank axis extensions are justified modern styling, not asserted source-raster facts.",
        "Existing current render/preview receipts prove 640x560 complete media, 22 px minimum transformed text, no collisions, and mobile end scrollLeft 282 for scrollWidth 640/clientWidth 358. This reviewer did not rerun or newly measure the display.",
        "PASS is restricted to this hash-bound current candidate. Durable rebinding, byte-identical promotion, one standard review record, and later edition/product acceptance remain parent-owned."
      ],
